WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.810
- There it drops.

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:03.240
18.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.210
- [Narrator] Depending on where you live,

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:05.970
getting the vaccine means the chance

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:07.890
at a check like this.

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:09.460
- That's right, you could win $1 million.

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:13.950
- How about a chance to
win a million dollars?

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:18.950
- The winner each Wednesday
will receive $1 million.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:21.420
- [Narrator] Faced with
falling vaccination rates,

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.930
states across the US

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:25.320
are rolling out incentives
to get residents

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.840
to roll up their sleeves.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:27.673
- Are we ready?

00:00:27.673 --> 00:00:29.510
- [Narrator] But are these offers working

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:31.050
and are they worth the cost?

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.473
- Stay safe, Ohio.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:35.120
- We needed to just shake things up.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.360
We needed to bring some excitement

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:40.680
and I felt that a million dollars

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.460
would bring excitement.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:44.190
- [Reporter] What a night it is for you.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:45.870
- [Narrator] Lotteries
like this one in Ohio

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.380
are part of a ballooning list

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.620
of vaccine incentives

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:51.710
that has included free
doughnuts, free beer,

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:53.500
fishing licenses, baseball tickets,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.280
a lap around Talladega Superspeedway and.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:00.720
- We're gonna give five
custom hunting rifles

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:05.080
and five custom hunting shotguns away.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.150
- [Narrator] Many of these freebies

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:08.310
and lotteries started
popping up last month

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:10.640
as the rate of vaccination
in the US slumped

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.830
to about half of what it
was at its peak in April.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.650
- It's not surprising
that we've reached a point

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:18.510
where the supply of
vaccines far exceeds demand

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.090
and it's time to start getting creative

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:21.600
about how to get some of the stragglers

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:22.620
over the finish line.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:23.610
But at the same time,

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:24.920
we have to be very clear eyed

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.140
about what these incentives
can and can't do.

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:29.705
- How you y'all doing?
- Hey, how are you?

00:01:29.705 --> 00:01:30.960
- [Narrator] When Ohio
Governor Mike DeWine announced

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.140
the Vax-a-Million Lottery on May 12th,

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:34.430
it was the first of its kind,

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:35.500
offering adults a chance

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.760
to win one of five one
million dollar prizes

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:39.270
and teens a chance to win one

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.270
of five full-ride scholarships.

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:44.720
- We were going down, down, down.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.480
And we couldn't break it.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:48.320
And no matter what we did.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.080
So we didn't know what else to do.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.977
So we came up with this idea,

00:01:51.977 --> 00:01:54.815
having no guarantee that it would work.

00:01:54.815 --> 00:01:57.010
- [Narrator] Experts
like Dr. Emily Largent,

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:58.560
who researches how incentives

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.730
are used in medical studies say lotteries

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:02.685
won't motivate everyone.

00:02:02.685 --> 00:02:03.633
- This is not a cure-all,

00:02:03.633 --> 00:02:05.060
this is something fun,

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.376
it makes sense to try

00:02:06.376 --> 00:02:08.630
but we shouldn't count on this

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:10.243
as being the magic bullet.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.780
- [Narrator] Recent
polling shows about 12%

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:14.800
of Americans still plan to wait and see

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.770
before getting the vaccine.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:18.660
Of those, only a small number said

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.020
they would be motivated to do so

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:21.390
by guaranteed incentives

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:22.880
like $100 from their state

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:25.590
or free tickets to a
sporting event or concert.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:26.720
These offers and lotteries

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.310
may even trigger the opposite response.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:30.500
- In some instances,

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:31.870
offering large amounts of money

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:34.970
to do something that
people perceive as risky

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:37.210
or burdensome can make them
feel like it's even riskier

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:39.440
or more burdensome than it actually is.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.950
- [Narrator] Some lawmakers
call these cash offers a bribe.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:43.900
But Dr. Largent says she's not worried

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:47.420
about these incentives taking
away an individual's choice.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:48.253
- The bigger concerns really are

00:02:48.253 --> 00:02:50.160
that they can distract from all the work

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.120
that needs to be going in

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.450
to trying to promote
vaccination in the community.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:56.019
- [Narrator] That includes
providing further education

00:02:56.019 --> 00:02:58.110
and access to vaccines.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.260
The lottery, she says, should only be part

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:03.430
of a broader toolkit
to promote vaccination.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:06.000
But if these incentives
are the right use of money

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.460
is heavily debated.

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:09.800
In Ohio's case, the $5 million lottery

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.760
was pulled from federal
coronavirus relief funds.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:14.450
- I knew at the time that we announced it,

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:16.900
people were gonna say, "DeWine is crazy."

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:19.240
They were gonna say
that's a waste of money.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:22.270
But the real waste is for
people to continue to die.

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:23.920
- [Narrator] Ohio resident, Jessica Nagy,

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:26.190
who got her shot before
the lottery announcement

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:27.423
says the money was well spent.

00:03:27.423 --> 00:03:29.810
- It could have spent on advertising

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.880
or marketing to educate
people on the vaccine

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.770
but I mean, how effective
would that really be

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:36.500
when anybody can get on Facebook

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.280
or social media and
say anything they want?

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.570
- I got my COVID vaccine.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.037
- So have I.
- I have too.

00:03:41.037 --> 00:03:41.950
- [Narrator] But so far,

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.280
Ohio has spent more than $11 million

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:47.160
on traditional advertising
to promote vaccination.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.160
- Taking a relatively
small amount of money

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.890
in the scheme of things,

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:53.670
like $5 million for incentives in Ohio

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.097
and offering it in this way

00:03:55.097 --> 00:03:56.650
that's drawn so much attention

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:58.350
has a real multiplier effect.

00:03:58.350 --> 00:03:59.350
This has drawn attention

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:02.920
not only in the State
of Ohio but nationally.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:04.390
- Ohio Governor Mike DeWine

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:05.493
has unlocked a secret.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:07.193
- [Narrator] In the week leading up

00:04:07.193 --> 00:04:08.420
to the lottery announcement,

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:13.070
Ohio averaged 13,400 new
vaccinations a day, then.

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:14.640
- A couple days after we announced it,

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:17.560
we were starting to see
in our numbers going up.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:18.700
- [Narrator] In the week following,

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.940
an average of 26,500 Ohioans

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:23.750
were getting their first shot each day,

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.380
a number caveated by the fact

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:28.210
that teens aged 12 to
15 were newly eligible

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.580
for the vaccine.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:33.130
But still, the state reported
a 28% week-over-week increase

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:35.170
in vaccination rates among those 16

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.710
and older the weekend
after the announcement.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.350
- Incentives make sense for some people.

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:42.160
They're likely to be
motivating for individuals

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:44.300
who are say young and healthy.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.150
Though vaccination,
they're not opposed to it,

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:48.100
but it's not really a priority for them.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.961
So offering something
that is a tangible benefit

00:04:50.961 --> 00:04:53.410
can help get them there sooner.

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:55.300
- [Narrator] Nagy had
initially planned to wait

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:57.730
to get her 12 and
14-year-olds their shots.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.790
- With myself, I thought a lot
more comfortable just going

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:01.710
and getting the vaccine with my kids.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.230
I did kinda wanna see
like nothing popping up

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:07.037
like crazy side effects
or anything like that.

00:05:07.037 --> 00:05:09.045
- [Narrator] But after
hearing about Vax-a-Million.

00:05:09.045 --> 00:05:10.300
- I thought why not?

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.200
A free ride to college sounds great.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:13.033
Why wait?

00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:14.700
I knew I was gonna probably do it anyway,

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.440
so yeah, I thought that would be awesome.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.640
So I just went ahead
and got 'em vaccinated.

00:05:20.857 --> 00:05:23.640
- [Narrator] That said, momentum
from the campaign in Ohio

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:24.790
may be slowing.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.050
In the week following the drawing

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:26.940
of the first winner,

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:29.210
the state's daily average
of new vaccinations

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:31.320
was back down to about 11,000.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:32.780
- I think seeing the winners out there

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:36.590
is gonna continue to
generate some excitement

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:38.070
but if it doesn't do anything else

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.829
besides what it's already
done, it's been worth it.

00:05:40.829 --> 00:05:42.390
- [Narrator] One potential downside

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:45.180
for states offering big prizes still looms

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:47.250
as it appears increasingly likely boosters

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:50.674
will be needed to maintain
protection from the virus.

00:05:50.674 --> 00:05:51.507
- We talk about the spoonful

00:05:51.507 --> 00:05:52.970
of sugar helping the medicine go down

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:55.770
but if you can only get
people to take the medicine

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:58.610
with the sugar, you have
habituated them to that.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:00.500
We might be creating a precedent now

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.720
for something that can be expensive

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.980
and potentially inefficient in the future.

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:05.930
- [Narrator] Setting a precedent

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:07.550
doesn't worry Governor DeWine

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:10.060
who's focused on getting shots in arms now

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:12.960
as his state still lags
behind the national average.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:14.210
- Not every decision we've made

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:16.160
has been write but it's been based

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:20.540
on the best facts that we could gather.

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:22.990
And so are we gonna
offer this in the future?

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:24.120
I don't know.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:27.810
But we're gonna continue
to do what it takes

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:30.330
to knock this virus down.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:32.160
- [Narrator] As she did with
her initial vaccination,

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:34.310
Nagy says she won't wait for an incentive

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:35.690
before getting a booster.

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:37.130
- Yeah, I definitely wouldn't expect it

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:38.950
but if it happens, great.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:40.823
A happy correlation.

